{"c":[{"id":"ec16c4fb792e99cf","sum":"W3-B29: XPCHostLink sends nothing before a verified reply; push v2/* only to sam; never-typed kinds only in memory/sensitive.ts; sockets need SO_NOSIGPIPE; Jev confidence = top-two margin; routed producers hold offers; scope words are allowlists; read-back diff = mayIncludeInput.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"48eb9dd5962c5d4c","sum":"W3-B26: XPCHostLink sends nothing until a verified reply; MemoryStore grants no authority; push v2/* only to sam; never-typed kinds only in memory/sensitive.ts; sockets need SO_NOSIGPIPE; Jev confidence = top-two margin; Groq 8k tok/min, space calls with fresh AbortSignal.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"ff412afe096d8651","sum":"W3/B25: XPCHostLink sends nothing until a verified reply; MemoryStore(dir) uses <dir>/Memory and grants no authority; oxc needs   escaped. Push v2/* only to sam. Intents gpt-oss-120b, plans qwen3.8 (~1k out tok/min); space writer calls with a fresh AbortSignal.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"c539feeaf5360a4d","sum":"W3: XPCHostLink sends nothing until a verified reply. Memory markdown: MemoryStore(dir) uses <dir>/Memory (real folder only without --data-dir) and grants no authority (that stays in memory.sqlite). oxc rejects raw U+2028 in a regex; write \\u2028.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"569740c12f8fdab5","sum":"W3: client setCodeSigningRequirement blocks what it receives, not its first call; XPCHostLink sends nothing until a verified reply. Memory is markdown: MemoryStore(dir) uses <dir>/Memory; main.ts uses the real folder only without --data-dir.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T204321Z-a08d2817ff5ece3d","text":"W3: NSXPCConnection.setCodeSigningRequirement on the client blocks what it receives, not its own first call; whoever owns the Mach name sees open's arguments, so XPCHostLink sends nothing until a verified reply.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T204904Z-98cc6d5ebfceb30a","text":"Personal memory is markdown (helper/src/memory): MemoryStore(dir) keeps it in <dir>/Memory unless told otherwise, and main.ts uses ~/Library/Application Support/Caret/Memory only when --data-dir is not given, so tests and evals never open the real folder.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"6e639a4926698b7e","sum":"Memory markdown grants no authority (permissions, onItsOwn, hand-off stay in memory.sqlite); editing a skill file puts it back on Tab (SkillJson.fileDigest). oxc rejects a raw U+2028/U+2029 in a regex literal; write the \\u2028 escape (Write tools may unescape it).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T204920Z-024f4219fb18c6cf","text":"Memory markdown grants no authority: permissions and a skill's onItsOwn, clean runs and hand-off stay in memory.sqlite; editing a skill's file puts it back on Tab, and SkillJson.fileDigest catches edits made while Caret was stopped.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T204920Z-0ba29fff62387456","text":"vite's oxc parser rejects a regex literal holding a raw U+2028/U+2029 (a line terminator); write the \\u2028 escape. An agent's Write tool can turn the escape into the raw character.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e60e3e751e2435c2","sum":"Remotes and Groq writers: push v2/* only to remote sam; Ask intents use gpt-oss-120b, plan programs qwen3.8 (about 1,000 output tokens a minute and 200k a day); space writer calls with a fresh AbortSignal after each wait. U+2731 marks required labels on the job form.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"e2ebd6c0099fdfde","sum":"Push v2/* only to remote sam (SamGu-NRX/Caret); origin is the team hackathon repo. Ask intents use INTENT_ROUTE (gpt-oss-120b), plan programs WRITER_ROUTE (qwen3.8, ~1,000 output tokens/min, 200k/day on Groq); gpt-oss strict json_schema can 400.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T210855Z-22a0908ac8155d26","text":"Push v2/* branches to the remote named sam (SamGu-NRX/Caret), where their PRs live. origin is the team hackathon repo (theodorexli/hackathon-2026-09-19); a bare 'git push origin' publishes there.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T211051Z-2bd567d78f578d5c","text":"B25: Ask intents go to INTENT_ROUTE (gpt-oss-120b), plan programs to WRITER_ROUTE (qwen3.8); qwen3.8's Groq 200k tokens/day ran out during dev runs, and gpt-oss strict json_schema can 400 'does not match the expected schema'.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b1d476e32a92cb95","sum":"B25: writers that space calls must give each request a fresh AbortSignal after the wait (a 15 s gap aborted every call); the job form marks required labels with U+2731, which realfill normLabel strips.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T211051Z-3925313f151b5275","text":"B25: eval writers that space calls must give the request a fresh AbortSignal after the wait; a 15 s gap aborted every intent in planner-eval's first GUI run.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T211051Z-9174d67891bff255","text":"B25: the job form marks required labels with U+2731; realfill normLabel strips it, and B24's scoreboards counted those four fields as not found.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0039d51d111ccafa","sum":"B25-B26/D2-02: never-typed kinds only in memory/sensitive.ts; bridge sockets need SO_NOSIGPIPE; Ask sentences in planner/says.ts; Jev 'confidence' is the top-two margin; Groq gpt-oss-120b allows 8k tok/min (space Ask evals 30 s); a one-token Groq probe hides a spent day.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"97c4b1112eed6f12","sum":"B25/W4/B26: never-typed kinds only in memory/sensitive.ts; captcha frames via compose.ts unit tests; bridge sockets need SO_NOSIGPIPE; a one-token Groq probe hides a spent day.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"e7d7ded421a71b5d","sum":"B25/W4: never-typed kinds live only in memory/sensitive.ts (extend it, no second list). HSTS-preloaded captcha hosts can't be pointed at a local server; test captcha frames via extension/src/worker/compose.ts unit tests.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T211051Z-bc8230171f42cb4e","text":"B25: never-typed kinds (fill, planner, Ask) are memory/sensitive.ts, M1's classifier copied unchanged from v2/memory; extend that file, never a second list.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T220624Z-f865060dd10d04a3","text":"W4: hcaptcha/recaptcha hosts are HSTS-preloaded, so --host-resolver-rules cannot point a test browser's captcha frame at a local http server (the load hangs); test captcha frame composition through extension/src/worker/compose.ts unit tests instead.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1c32ace5fe4e098f","sum":"W4/B26: bridge test sockets a fixture accept()s need SO_NOSIGPIPE or signal 13 kills the run. Groq answers a one-token probe after a model's daily tokens run out; only a real-size request shows the 429.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T223033Z-e64c70b59e406a7f","text":"W4: Swift Testing runs bridge tests in one process; a test socket that a fixture accept()s needs SO_NOSIGPIPE, or a write after the peer closed kills the whole run with signal 13, blamed on whichever test was running.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T224111Z-04a43869ad872043","text":"B26: Groq answers a one-token probe even when a model's tokens-per-day is spent; only a real-size request shows the 429 TPD. gpt-oss-120b's day ran out during B26's first Ask run.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"78eeba3d0e4f7ab9","sum":"B26/D2-02: Ask sentences live in planner/says.ts; generator measurements pin setGeneratorClock; Jev 'confidence' is the top-two margin; Groq gpt-oss-120b allows 8k tokens/min, so Ask evals space calls 30 s.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"943dffc1dbc84f96","sum":"B26: Ask refusals and questions live in planner/says.ts (SaidError message for the user, detail for ids and provider errors); offline generator measurements must pin setGeneratorClock or cold forms hit the time budget.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T224111Z-32ca3d0fc6e98438","text":"B26: every Ask refusal or question sentence lives in planner/says.ts; a SaidError's message is what the user reads and its detail holds the check's text (ids, provider errors). Scoreboards print both.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T224111Z-6a820f7b64075f54","text":"B26: offline generator measurements (scripts/realfill-budgets.ts and the like) must pin setGeneratorClock, or cold first forms are cut short by the time budget and the numbers vary run to run.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"47481f5f6fb24ec8","sum":"D2-02: Jev Choice 'confidence' is the top-two margin (0.75 needs ~0.875 on the winner); Groq gpt-oss-120b, the Ask intent writer, allows 8,000 tokens/min, so Ask evals space calls 30 s.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T233505Z-310484d235184787","text":"D2-02: Jev Choice 'confidence' is the margin between the top two option probabilities (raw answers also carry 'probabilities'); a 0.75 floor needs about 0.875 on the winner.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T233506Z-254786afcaf981c8","text":"D2-02: Groq gpt-oss-120b (the Ask intent writer) allows 8,000 tokens a minute; an intent is about 2,000, so Ask evals space calls 30 s or get 429 'unavailable'.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b4fb8385e296a602","sum":"D2-02..B29: routed producers hold offers (await routing.idle); fixtures await waitForLoad after navigating; scope words are allowlists, exclusion words end name trust; controls ride FillHandoff; boxes tick only for a question; differing read-back sets mayIncludeInput.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"077248175b9b025f","sum":"D2-02/B27/B28: routed producers hold offers until chosen; Router 1 answers near the 0.5 floor flip between runs; score B17/B18 with b27/memsets relabels; fixtures need waitForLoad after navigation; Ask scope words are scope-words.ts allowlists.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"bae047d115123a98","sum":"D2-02/B27: no routing = producers self-trigger; routed producers hold offers until chosen (await routing.idle, routedSettled). Router 1 answers within ~0.05 of the 0.5 floor flip run to run; diff per moment. Failed fills reach the user only via Helper.fillFailed.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"3ae20362fc05a5eb","sum":"D2-02/B27: routing absent keeps producers self-triggering; routed producers hold offers until chosen (await routing.idle then routedSettled). B17/B18 memory held-out sets label own First/Last 'none'; score with relabelled copies in evidence/screen/b27/memsets.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T233521Z-ca79b84757c7cc74","text":"D2-02: HelperOptions.routing absent keeps producers self-triggering (tests, producer evals); main.ts routes when Jev is on. Routed producers hold offers (engine.release/dropHeld, openApp.showHeld, events.judge); await routing.idle() then routedSettled.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T235441Z-17480ff5b594d902","text":"B27: B17/B18 memory held-out sets label the user's own First/Last name fields 'none' (written when fill copied values only whole); score them with the relabelled copies in ~/.caret-run/evidence/screen/b27/memsets, whose about-fill-eval accepts expect first/last.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ccba801a8aa9c8ea","sum":"D2-02/B27: Router 1 answers within ~0.05 of the 0.5 floor flip between live corpus runs; diff runs per moment before crediting a code change. A failed fill reaches the user only via Helper.fillFailed (planner/says.ts fillSays); ids go to warn.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T031924Z-459c6ef9ec89ae5d","text":"D2-02: Router 1 answers within ~0.05 of its 0.5 floor flip between live corpus runs (m02 0.52/0.49, m09 0.45/0.51); diff runs per moment before crediting a code change with a recall move.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T032639Z-5905894b0fafbfcc","text":"B27: a failed fill reaches the user only through Helper.fillFailed (planner/says.ts fillSays); its window and field ids go to warn. Early exits that called this.error published ids until afadd34.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"9e36f49db21c9173","sum":"B28 web-form fixtures: wait for site.waitForLoad after a navigation before the next site.command; accept.ts can't use executor.run (native watchInput gives noWindow); Ask scope words are scope-words.ts allowlists.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"91fb33162eeab888","sum":"B28: after a fixture page navigates away, wait for site.waitForLoad of the landed page before the next site.command, or it hits the departing page's long poll and times out. (B28's 'accept.ts cannot run executor.run' was lifted in D2-04.)","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T044215Z-74ca06dede7d18b3","text":"B28: after a fixture page navigates away, wait for site.waitForLoad of the landed page before the next site.command, or the command goes to the departing page's long poll and times out.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T044215Z-8ef7ae66324e8796","text":"B28: accept.ts cannot run executor.run: it first asks the native reader for watchInput and gets noWindow; check page-link VerbResults in accept and the executor with test/fake-app.ts knobs.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e2fcc93ff7d0331d","sum":"B28: Ask scope words (planner/scope-words.ts) are allowlists: a whole-form or section scope counts only if the whole instruction is a scope-words grammar sentence. Matching labels or searching inside failed open 8 times.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T044915Z-bf6a7f62ff27c59b","text":"B28: Ask scope words (planner/scope-words.ts) are allowlists: only FILLER may stand beside a whole-form or section phrase, and a source phrase must open with a preposition. Matching field labels in the rest failed open three times.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T060231Z-5982020e0a78f148","text":"B28: Ask trusts a whole-form or section scope only if the whole normalized instruction is a scope-words.ts grammar sentence, and a section only under one un-nested heading that is wholly the user's own. Searching inside after stripping sources/titles/quotes failed open 5 times.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"16aeb5fd1a76ee7a","sum":"B28b/D2-04/B29: exclusion words drop name trust; boxes tick only for a question label; controls never ride FillField.value; ledger 'after' is intended, differing read-back = mayIncludeInput; number undo compares numerically; RESTRICTS matches 'without using X'.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"c6f40c96b6283efc","sum":"B28b/D2-04: EXCLUSION_WORDS end name trust; SECTION trusts only fields of its meaning. A control's value never rides FillField.value. A box gets a tick only for a question to the user (boxKind). accept.ts runs executor tasks on page windows.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"6936d2244b2292af","sum":"B28b: an Ask with an EXCLUSION_WORDS word (scope-words.ts) gets no name trust; a SECTION phrase trusts only fields of its meaning. D2-04: a control's value never goes on the wire as FillField.value; Fill all writes controls whose FillHandoff.writes is true.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T063813Z-3bd79ae87e6b8e79","text":"B28b: an Ask instruction with a scope-words.ts EXCLUSION_WORDS word gets no name trust (Jev confirms every field); a SECTION phrase trusts only fields of its meaning (isContactField; up top, my details: none). Restriction word lists stay open; each review found more.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T080809Z-f16da6d6064b889b","text":"D2-04: a control's value never goes on the wire as FillField.value (zod and the host decoder refuse it on any control but text); a Fill all writes the controls whose FillHandoff.writes is true, through writtenFields.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"4fad04d8f129b479","sum":"D2-04: a box gets a tick only when its label is a question to the user (fill/controls.ts boxKind); never widen it by adding consent words. accept.ts's fixture reader answers watchInput ok, so accept runs executor tasks on page windows.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T080829Z-0265fdcfcf17917c","text":"D2-04: a box gets a tick by its label's kind (fill/controls.ts boxKind: only a question to the user may be written, a first-person statement never gets a value); consent word lists failed open in both reviews, so never widen the box rule by adding words alone.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T080829Z-0557296abbc22e11","text":"D2-04: accept.ts's fixture reader answers watchInput ok, so accept now runs executor tasks on page windows (B28's 'accept cannot run executor.run' no longer holds); page input still comes from the extension's guard.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b8f8d8cc08d8e1b1","sum":"D2-04/B29: radio peers found tree-wide by name+form owner; ledger 'after' is the intended value, a differing read-back sets mayIncludeInput (undo refuses); number fields compare numerically for undo only; RESTRICTS matches 'without using X' (tests say 'not from X').","tree":{"c":[{"id":"50990865af94b806","sum":"D2-04: find a radio's peers tree-wide by name and form owner (the form attribute). B29: an executor write's ledger 'after' is the intended value; a differing read-back sets mayIncludeInput and undo refuses it, as for pre-B29 rows.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T080829Z-c2d09e45a7621952","text":"D2-04: find a radio's peers tree-wide by name and form owner: a button outside its form element joins it through the form attribute. The walker's radioPeers and the content script's otherChecked both searched the form element only.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T092126Z-f0c295d458383a43","text":"B29: an executor write's ledger 'after' is the value Caret meant to write; a read-back that differs sets mayIncludeInput and undo refuses it. Journal rows without afterIntended (saved before B29) recover their confirmed writes as mayIncludeInput.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"33a32dbecb06c39a","sum":"B29: page number fields compare as numbers for undo identity only (executor.ts canonicalDecimal, not Number()); sources.ts RESTRICTS also matches 'without using X' (no source question), so excluded-window tests say 'not from X'.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T092127Z-2a54c50194565255","text":"B29: page number fields (type=number, inputmode numeric/decimal -> PAGE_SUBROLE.number) compare as numbers for undo identity only, through executor.ts canonicalDecimal; Number() made 9007199254740993 equal 9007199254740992.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T092127Z-2d5fb1876e453777","text":"B29: sources.ts RESTRICTS also matches 'without using X', and such an instruction gets no source question; tests of an excluded source window use 'not from X'.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"99ceec73726b21c8","sum":"B29-P2: continued Asks refuse a changed form (fieldSeen); only digest goalAccept runs goal steps; drafts.ts whole typed facts; goals done only with left[] empty, writes pass gates.ts; no default chat route; no-groq.ts guard; heads maker gated as one answer.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"dc7d188142ab25ed","sum":"B29-R3: continued Asks refuse a changed form (fieldSeen); only a digest goalAccept runs goal steps; writes skip Cc/Bcc/Subject. drafts.ts: whole typed facts, no token lists. Jev: judged text in state, rules in instructions; R3 evals use the fake clock.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"35936a7e83eb504c","sum":"B29-B30/D2-06: a continued Ask refuses a changed form (ask.ts fieldSeen); page presses are hand-offs; only a digest-named goalAccept runs goal steps (Target.exact); GoalRuns.blocked is null once a segment ends; goal writes skip Cc/Bcc/Subject, To = answered From.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"73cd22e0cad86c6d","sum":"B29/D2-06: a continued Ask refuses a changed form by ask.ts fieldSeen; choice questions go only to askChoices consumers. Page presses are hand-offs; only a goalAccept with its digest runs goal steps, never taskControl; goal targets are Target.exact.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"1c75543de1b1c0e8","sum":"B29: a continued Ask refuses a changed form by ask.ts fieldSeen (before and after fill's Jev calls): add to fieldSeen whatever fill starts reading. Questions with choices go only to a consumer whose hello lists askChoices; others read AskRefused's sentence.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T092127Z-2ff420afa6ce639a","text":"B29: a continued Ask refuses a changed form by ask.ts fieldSeen, checked before and after the fill's Jev calls; three reviews each found something fill reads that the record missed, so add to fieldSeen whatever fill starts reading.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T092127Z-c755285b7eff0669","text":"B29: Ask questions with choices (planner/choices.ts) go only to a consumer whose hello lists askChoices; AskAsks extends AskRefused, so any other caller reads the old refusal sentence.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"cf5de0df55b6d70e","sum":"D2-06: 'Continue' stays unclassified; the one goal press is e:reveal on a whole 'Next'; page presses are hand-offs. Only a goalAccept (goalId, segment, digest) runs goal steps; a goal task is never resumed by taskControl; goal targets are Target.exact.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T105430Z-1712f90f65a11b14","text":"D2-06: 'Continue' is deliberately unclassified at every press boundary (it confirms destructive macOS dialogs); the one goal press capability is e:reveal on a whole 'Next' (goals/capabilities.ts). Page presses are always hand-offs.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T105430Z-1ba2dff3c7f2e7e3","text":"D2-06: only a goalAccept (goalId, segment, digest) runs a goal's steps; a goal task (GoalRuns.owns) is never resumed by taskControl, and a pause stops it. Goal targets are Target.exact (key+role, a button's label): resolveLocally never falls back for them.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"046b14781a65d0ff","sum":"D2-06/B30: GoalRuns.blocked must return null once a segment ends, or undo is refused; a goal host's plan Ask comes back as AskGoal. Keep name patterns case-sensitive; goal writes never touch Cc/Bcc/Subject, and To takes only the answered message's From.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"24a976c12b8a54f1","sum":"D2-06/B30: GoalRuns.blocked (inside Helper.authorize) must return null once a segment ends, or undo is refused. A goal host's Ask with route plan comes back as AskGoal (planAsk goals:true) for helper.offerGoal; other consumers keep planTask/planWithCode.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T105431Z-2d9978b4db29946e","text":"D2-06: GoalRuns.blocked runs inside Helper.authorize before every act; it must return null once a segment ends, or a goal task's undo (undoBlocked -> authorize) is refused.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T120548Z-9e86109ce30422ae","text":"B30: a goal-planning host's Ask with route plan is offered as a D2-06 goal (planAsk goals:true returns AskGoal; helper.offerGoal); other consumers keep planTask/planWithCode. planAsk overloads: goals absent/false types as AskDraft.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b7329c13cd423b17","sum":"B30: keep name patterns case-sensitive (the i flag folds \\p{Lu}). Goal writes never touch Cc/Bcc or Subject; To takes only the From of the message the reply answers, rechecked at accept (drafts.ts senderOf); D2-06 scenes need mailWindow line 0 to be From.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T120548Z-b6135cb945f89335","text":"B30: JS regex with the i flag folds \\p{Lu} to match lower case too; a case-insensitive name pattern let 'Thanks, I'll pay' skip Jev. Keep name patterns case-sensitive.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T120548Z-c27c662d572bf540","text":"B30: goal writes never touch Cc/Bcc or Subject, and To takes only the From address in the header block of the message the reply window answers (Re: <subject>), rechecked at accept (drafts.ts senderOf). D2-06 scenes rely on mailWindow line 0 being its From header.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"27eaa3d887b9c175","sum":"B30/R2/R3: drafts.ts checks goal text as whole typed facts (no token allowlists); replayed typing carries its value and focusedKey in one snapshot. Jev: what it judges in state, rules in instructions; R3 evals: fake clock, await a flush.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"08019c2469975896","sum":"B30: drafts.ts checks drafted text as whole typed facts; fix holes with whole-expression rules, never token allowlists. R2: replayed typing carries its typed value in the text's snapshot, with focusedKey; Router 1 is skipped only for consented held-offer records from a host.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"60828e069b1c490e","sum":"B30: drafts.ts checks drafted goal text as whole typed facts (every digit in a fact; a from ref stands for its source); fix holes with whole-expression rules, never token allowlists. R2: replayed typing must carry its typed value in the same snapshot as its text.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T120623Z-4f068d6de508aa09","text":"B30: drafted goal text is checked in goals/drafts.ts as whole typed facts; every digit must land in a fact, and a from value ref stands for its source window or memory. Two reviews found recombination holes: add whole-expression rules, never token allowlists.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T155131Z-2d735fed11dec073","text":"R2: scripts that replay typing must send a typed value (snapshot values) in the same snapshot as its text: a value that arrives after the sentence boundary opens no breakpoint, so the event card is never listed.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"9774fe46b42d75d6","sum":"R2: recorded snapshots need the reader's focusedKey or Router 1 abstains (A5's offers-loop.ndjson until 831ab47). Router 1 is skipped only for Helper.consentedCandidates offers on a held offer's own record; messages writing such records count only from a host session.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T155131Z-b3055d198779a6ea","text":"R2: a recorded snapshot without the reader's focusedKey makes Router 1 read 'the cursor is not in a text field' and abstain; A5's offers-loop.ndjson lacked it until 831ab47, which is why H6 saw the loop abstain.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T155145Z-05c6fed3ed39acff","text":"R2: Router 1 is skipped only for offers Helper.consentedCandidates builds on a held offer's own record (routing/consent.ts). Messages that write such records (skillAnswer, resume, skills/ save, watch role) count only from a host session.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"34b44a5905bccdea","sum":"R3: put what Jev judges in state, the rule in instructions; Router 1's task question is its own request. corpus-eval --real-clock skips the cooldown timer (use the fake clock); with jev.holding await a flush, not coord.idle().","tree":{"c":[{"id":"ce9d88d32e0d9097","sum":"R3: corpus-eval --real-clock settle() skips the router cooldown timer, so run incoming-line moments on the fake clock; with jev.holding a stale reply frees the slot and the next call starts at once, so await a flush, not coord.idle().","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T170330Z-3e0249266797e51f","text":"R3: corpus-eval --real-clock settle() does not wait the router cooldown timer, so an incoming line's later context is never scored; run incoming-line moments on the fake clock.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T170330Z-4f977dd1bf6c45f7","text":"R3: coordinator tests with jev.holding: a stale reply now frees the slot and the next field's call starts at once, so await a flush, not coord.idle(), while a call is held (idle would wait on the held call).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7d9ef00b5bb5eb15","sum":"R3: Jev judges state against short criteria: put what it judges in state, the rule in instructions (sentence inside the act option split 8/14 vs 14/14). Router 1's task question is its own request after outcome; one shared state moved outcomes (m34 write 0.75 -> 0.32).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T170330Z-539f47d0a41290db","text":"R3: Jev (System One) judges the request state against short criteria; put what it judges in state and the rule in instructions. Router 1's task question with the sentence inside the act option split ~50/50 (r3 task-wording probe 8/14 vs 14/14).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T170330Z-75585e5911775e88","text":"R3: Router 1's task question (judge.ts) is its own request after the outcome question; with the offer in one shared state the outcome answers moved (corpus m34 write 0.75 -> 0.32).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"4284f1ca9dc73cce","sum":"R3/G2/L1/P1/P2: event-card misses are producer code; goal done only with left[] empty; goal writes pass gates.ts; never widen restates(); no default chat route; Gemma E2B few-shot+grammar; no-groq.ts guard; new Ask makers join planAsk's one-answer gate.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"920b76cc0b40179f","sum":"R3/G2/L1: event-card misses are event-card code; 'unknown' selection reads as caret; a goal is done only with left[] empty; goal writes pass gates.ts (desk tests: standInJev); never widen drafts.ts restates(); D2-06 scene 2 partial live; no default chat route.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"ba466bbf79b5d07e","sum":"R3/G2: corpus event-card misses are producer code, not the router; context.ts reads 'unknown' selection as a caret. A goal is finished only with left[] empty; goal values are picked by their quoted part, not display.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"362f7f2441a3fcab","sum":"R3: corpus m36/m43 miss event cards by the producer's rule (relative date, no anchor), m37 finds no person: event-card code, not the router. routing/context.ts treats the helper's 'unknown' selection as a caret, since RouteFollower sends none then.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T170330Z-9c33f255f5c1caad","text":"R3: corpus m36/m43 list no event card by the producer's rule (a conversation line's relative date has no anchor); m37 finds no person. Those misses are event-card code, not the router.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T170330Z-dcc2d733c48b884a","text":"R3: RouteFollower sends no routingContext while the selection is a plain caret, so routing/context.ts treats the helper's 'unknown' selection as caret; comparing them ended every write session at the host's first sentence end.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e516245b6d5f910e","sum":"G2: GoalProgress finished is done only with left[] empty; runs.ts owes every required or recipient field in windows a goal writes. A goal value's display names its source window, so goal-prompt.ts says pick values by their quoted part.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T173412Z-100b242cff553f5d","text":"G2: GoalProgress finished is done only when left[] is empty (partial/handoff otherwise); runs.ts owes every field left.ts marks required or recipient in windows a goal writes in, and a closed window leaves them unresolved.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T173412Z-33695164e4940cad","text":"G2: a goal value's display names its source window's title, so live qwen3.8 matched v.display.includes('ORD-...') to the sender's email; goal-prompt.ts now says pick values by their quoted part.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"6c61dbb360ed9d23","sum":"G2/L1: goal writes pass goals/gates.ts (lowerGoal async, needs askJev + ledger; desk tests use goal-desk.ts standInJev); never widen drafts.ts restates(); live Jev leaves D2-06 scene 2 partial; no chat route is a default (name groq:/gateway: via --dev-writer).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"8febf1c1fb5ea75f","sum":"G2: every goal write passes goals/gates.ts (never-typed, misfit, verifyWrites); with no Jev a goal writes no copied value (desk tests use goal-desk.ts standInJev). drafts.ts restates() is a closed-frame clause-suffix rule; never widen it by adding words.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T173412Z-c65516aec96de620","text":"G2: every goal write passes goals/gates.ts (never-typed, misfit + numberFieldMisfit, Ask's verifyWrites Jev question); lowerGoal is async and needs askJev + ledger; with no Jev a goal writes no copied value, so desk tests pass test/goal-desk.ts standInJev.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T173413Z-41b9cc8b0f0c0c83","text":"G2: drafts.ts restates() (skip Jev for a restated sentence) is a closed-frame clause-suffix rule; two reviews found 5 bypasses in looser versions (token sets, 'Avoid saying', 'NOT saying', 'provided'); never widen it by adding words.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e10542c624d65f47","sum":"G2: live Jev (0.75 floor) confirmed Order number but not a reply's sender in To or a derived event, so D2-06 scene 2 ends partial live (evidence/screen/g2). L1: no chat route is a default; developers name groq:<model> or gateway:<model> via --dev-writer.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T180513Z-82a90a8786c261a8","text":"G2: live Jev (Ask's yes/no value question, 0.75 floor) confirmed Order number but not a reply's sender in To or a derived calendar event for 'add this meeting to my calendar and draft a reply to Priya', so D2-06 scene 2 ends partial live; see evidence/screen/g2 jev-*-probe.txt.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T201333Z-b3e261779dc6c92b","text":"L1: no chat route is a default (WRITER_ROUTE and INTENT_ROUTE null, ASK_MAKER jev); a developer names one as groq:<model> or gateway:<model> (writer/routes.ts) with the helper's --dev-writer or an eval script's writer flag.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"5fee49e1dd2634c5","sum":"L1/P1/P2: Gemma E2B base model (few-shot, grammar, deadlineMs epoch ms); labelTooLong >80 chars; old hosts throw on unknown memoryDocument ids; no-groq.ts guard; heads maker gated as one answer in planAsk; recheckFill needs label context; 'Label:' parts carry it.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"31d09dcbe08a45f9","sum":"L1/P1: Gemma E2B base model (few-shot local drafts, grammar required, deadlineMs epoch ms); labelTooLong over 80-char focused labels on low-prose pages; old hosts throw on unknown memoryDocument ids; no-groq.ts fails tests reading GROQ_API_KEY.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"227c87230dc71c8a","sum":"L1: Gemma E2B is a base model (local draft prompts are few-shot; caret-local-model refuses a request with no grammar; deadlineMs is epoch ms). Fill throws labelTooLong for a focused label over 80 chars on a page with little prose.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T201333Z-fdcac01d5471b677","text":"L1: Cotypist's Gemma E2B is a base model, so local draft prompts are few-shot documents (writer/local-draft.ts); caret-local-model refuses a request with no grammar. localTextRequest.deadlineMs is epoch ms, not a duration.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T204550Z-12e324b0b44784bf","text":"Fill throws labelTooLong when the focused field's label is over 80 chars on a page with little other prose (privacy prose share); saved answers can't be offered there.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b818cff7ff0f8991","sum":"Hosts before v2/answers throw on an unknown memoryDocument id (answers.md is listed only to savedAnswers hosts). P1: test/setup/no-groq.ts fails any test reading process.env.GROQ_API_KEY; pass explicit env objects in tests.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T204550Z-3e3d4d7a0bdec136","text":"Hosts before v2/answers throw on an unknown memoryDocument id, losing the whole memory list; the server lists answers.md only to hosts with the savedAnswers capability.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T205140Z-7ef033e31edcf1b4","text":"P1: helper/test/setup/no-groq.ts (vitest setupFiles) fails any test file that reads process.env.GROQ_API_KEY, even if the throw is caught; pass explicit env objects to readKey/writersOnStart in tests.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"987201798448cfb5","sum":"P1/P2: recheckFill refused W4 Greenhouse whole (derived Country, no label context); add new Ask makers to planAsk's one-answer gate; parts from a 'Label:' line carry it as context; page-link patches verified writes into the last walk.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"091da897e0ecfee3","sum":"P1: recheckFill refused W4 Greenhouse Fill all whole (Country is a derived part; a control with no label context needs a line equal to its span). The heads Ask maker is one answer: planAsk gates it like the writer; add a new maker name to that gate.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T205140Z-d6ebebc54b7a4ea1","text":"P1: on W4's saved Greenhouse pages Fill all is refused whole by recheckFill (offers/fill-popup.ts ~218): Country 'United States' is a derived part of 'Location: Oakland, California, United States (...)', and a control without label context needs a line equal to the span.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T205140Z-f4ebc7703c97844e","text":"P1: the heads Ask maker (planner/intent-heads.ts) is one answer, so planAsk gates it like the writer (oneAnswer = makerName !== 'jev': inferredAll, listsAll, confirmScope); a new maker name must be added to that gate or its scope stands unconfirmed.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0584c276559db78d","sum":"P2: a part from one 'Label: value' line carries that label as context; recheckFields drops only failing fields; an unlabelled span in a longer line passes only if derive.ts re-derives it. page-link patches a verified write into the last walk, then walks once later.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T220819Z-519d2cf2c3af807c","text":"P2: a fill part derived from one 'Label: value' line carries that label as FillHandoff.context; recheckFields drops a field that fails its recheck and runs the rest; an unlabelled span inside a longer line passes only if derive.ts re-derives it (fill-popup.ts sourceHolds).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T220819Z-878907191e2eb647","text":"P2: engines/page-link.ts no longer walks after a verified pageWrite/pageSelect/pageSetChecked; it patches that control in the tab's last walk and walks once TRAILING_WALK_MS after the last act. Tests that expected a pageWalk after an ok write must expect the patch.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
